{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-instanton-unique","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:categorical-instanton-unique","kind":"proposition","title":"Uniqueness of categorical instantons (moduli)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-instanton-exists"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-categorical-instanton-unique"],"tags":["uniqueness","instanton","moduli"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalInstanton.unique_up_to_gauge","text":"categorical-instanton-unique.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-instanton-unique.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:categorical-instanton-unique\"></a><p>Two categorical instantons <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nabla_1</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nabla_2</code> of the same topological charge <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_2(\\nabla_i) = k \\in H^4</code> coincide up to a categorical gauge transformation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g \\in \\mathrm{Aut}^\\otimes(\\tau)</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\nabla_2 \\;=\\; g \\cdot \\nabla_1 \\cdot g^{-1} + g\\,dg^{-1}.</code></pre>\n<p>The categorical instanton moduli space <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{M}^{\\mathrm{inst}}_k</code> is parameterised by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H^4</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-instanton-unique.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"3.17.3"}
